<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Solador per-host metrics agent: the macOS LaunchDaemon (#506, part of #505).

  Generated by deploy/install.sh in its system-daemon mode from
  agent/deploy/app.solador.agent.daemon.plist, whose at-sign placeholders it
  renders (XML-escaped) into the paths it actually installed to. The install
  runs AS THE SERVICE USER and renders this file into that user's own home;
  it never writes /Library and never calls launchctl. Loading it is the one
  privileged step, which the installer prints for an operator to run: copy
  this file to /Library/LaunchDaemons as root:wheel mode 0644, then bootstrap
  it into the system domain. A LaunchDaemon, not a LaunchAgent: it starts at
  boot with nobody logged in, and runs as UserName below, never as root. That
  is the whole reason this template exists next to app.solador.agent.plist.

  Identical to that template except for UserName and GroupName (the service
  user and its primary group) and two more EnvironmentVariables, HOME and
  SOLADOR_AGENT_CONFIG_DIR. A daemon is not given the user's HOME the way a
  LaunchAgent is, and every path the agent derives (its state, its TLS
  keypair) is rooted in the service user's home, so both are set rather than
  inherited. It asks for no launchd session: the agent uses no keychain, and
  a session would only be a second thing to go wrong.

  ProgramArguments is the launcher, then the binary, the env file and the log
  file, in exactly that order, the shape the LaunchAgent template has and
  that the in-binary updater reads from that template. The updater (#507)
  reads this shape from /Library/LaunchDaemons, run as UserName, and restarts
  the daemon by SIGTERM to its own process, which KeepAlive relaunches: keep
  UserName, a binary under that user's home, KeepAlive and ThrottleInterval as
  they are. The bearer token is NOT here: the launcher reads the env file (mode 0600) at
  every start, so rotating it stays "edit that file, restart the service".

  PATH is set and load-bearing, for the reason the LaunchAgent template gives:
  launchd's compiled-in PATH holds none of docker, tart or podman, and an
  agent that cannot find a runtime serves /v1/containers as [] under a green
  /v1/health.

  KeepAlive + RunAtLoad is systemd's Restart=always; the throttle is launchd's
  RestartSec, and the updater's restart (a SIGTERM to the agent's own process, as
  UserName, never root) relies on KeepAlive to relaunch the agent. No ProcessType, for the timer-coalescing reason the
  LaunchAgent template records.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>@LABEL@</string>
    <key>UserName</key>
    <string>@USER@</string>
    <key>GroupName</key>
    <string>@GROUP@</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>@LAUNCHER@</string>
        <string>@BINARY@</string>
        <string>@ENV_FILE@</string>
        <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/podman/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>@HOME@</string>
        <key>SOLADOR_AGENT_CONFIG_DIR</key>
        <string>@CONFIG_DIR@</string>
    </dict>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>3</integer>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
</dict>
</plist>
